WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.872
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, November twenty fifth.

2
00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:12.570
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.088
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.088 --> 00:00:34.307
Today: an evacuation warning for Yemen's Hodeidah port and a Houthi threat against Saudi Red Sea ports, a hostage standoff in Cartagena, Colombia, drone strikes near Iranian Kurdish opposition camps in northern Iraq, a missing military aircraft in eastern Congo, and new Ebola screening rules for travelers to Malawi.

5
00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:35.642
We start in Yemen.

6
00:00:35.642 --> 00:00:41.327
Reuters reports the Saudi-led coalition issued an evacuation warning for Yemen's Hodeidah port.

7
00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:51.606
Reuters also reports the Houthis said the Saudi port of Jeddah and all other Saudi ports on the Red Sea coast would be targeted if Saudi Arabia carried out threats to attack Hodeidah.

8
00:00:51.606 --> 00:00:53.164
Next, Colombia.

9
00:00:53.164 --> 00:01:01.003
Reuters reports about twenty people were held hostage in a supermarket in Cartagena yesterday after a failed armored car hijacking.

10
00:01:01.003 --> 00:01:13.683
Colombian media, including El Colombiano and El Universo, report security forces rescued all of the hostages alive after more than fifteen hours, and that one of the hostage takers was killed in the operation.

11
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:17.460
President Abelardo de la Espriella praised the operation.

12
00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.129
Turning to northern Iraq.

13
00:01:19.129 --> 00:01:33.409
Rudaw English reports three one way attack drones struck near two camps of the Kurdistan Democratic Party of Iran in Erbil province yesterday evening, including the Azadi camp in Koya, according to a party official and a security source.

14
00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:35.401
No casualties were reported.

15
00:01:35.401 --> 00:01:43.463
In Congo, BBC Africa reports the government is searching for one of its aircraft after rebels said they shot down a warplane in the east.

16
00:01:43.463 --> 00:01:50.383
Local reports say the army lost contact with a Cessna cargo plane over South Kivu on Sunday, November twenty second, near Minembwe.

17
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:52.797
And in Malawi, the U.K.

18
00:01:52.797 --> 00:01:57.945
Foreign Office updated its travel advice with Malawi's Ebola screening measures.

19
00:01:57.945 --> 00:02:10.469
Travelers arriving from or transiting through Uganda, Kenya or Nigeria will be monitored daily for twenty one days, and travelers arriving from Congo must self isolate for twenty one days under daily monitoring.

20
00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:12.713
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:24.265
In Africa, ACLED says Ethiopian forces regained control of two locations near Badme on Monday, November twenty third, with Eritrean forces reportedly reducing their presence in the area.

22
00:02:24.265 --> 00:02:35.066
In Somalia, the Somali Guardian reports al-Shabaab released images of a destroyed armored vehicle it says belonged to a Ugandan military convoy it attacked in the Lower Shabelle region.

23
00:02:35.066 --> 00:02:44.339
In Europe, Russia's Federal Security Service says it foiled a planned attack on a synagogue in Kislovodsk, in southern Russia, according to i24NEWS.

24
00:02:44.339 --> 00:02:51.988
In Asia, Reuters reports North Korea expelled a Swiss diplomat over sanctions, weeks after the Swiss office reopened.

25
00:02:51.988 --> 00:03:03.797
On sanctions and terrorism listings, the George Washington University Program on Extremism reports Canada on Monday, November twenty third, added the group Masar Badil to its terrorist entity list as an alias of Samidoun.

26
00:03:03.797 --> 00:03:15.460
On cyber, The Record reports Britain's National Cyber Security Centre has observed a marked rise since September in cyberattacks assisted by artificial intelligence.

27
00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:23.508
The Record also reports Spain's professional soccer league, LaLiga, said hackers stole fans' personal information in a cyberattack.

28
00:03:23.508 --> 00:03:36.232
In the Middle East, the U.N. humanitarian office says some three hundred fifty thousand children in Taiz, Yemen, missed a national measles and rubella vaccination campaign because insecurity prevented vaccine delivery.

29
00:03:36.232 --> 00:03:37.671
That's today's brief.

30
00:03:37.671 --> 00:03:45.921
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

31
00:03:45.921 --> 00:03:54.237
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

32
00:03:54.237 --> 00:03:56.358
This brief is digitally narrated.

33
00:03:56.358 --> 00:03:57.327
Questions?

34
00:03:57.327 --> 00:04:00.840
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

35
00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.098
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
